# College Management System

A desktop-based College Management System developed using **Java Swing, JDBC and MySQL**. The application provides separate administrator and student interfaces to manage and access college records.

## Features

### Administrator Module
- Admin login and first-admin setup
- Create and manage administrator accounts
- Add, view and delete student records
- Add, view and delete faculty records
- Manage student attendance
- Add and view examination results
- Record and view fee details

### Student Module
- Student account creation and login
- View personal profile
- View attendance records
- View examination results
- View fee details

## Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Java | Application logic |
| Java Swing | Graphical User Interface |
| JDBC | Database connectivity |
| MySQL | Data storage |
| MySQL Connector/J | Java-MySQL integration |

## Project Structure

```text
College-Management-System/
│
├── src/
│   └── DBConnection.java
│
├── lib/
│   └── mysql-connector-j-26.10.0.jar
│
├── out/                 (Generated during compilation)
├── .gitignore
├── run.bat
└── README.md
```

## Prerequisites

- Java JDK installed
- MySQL Server installed and running
- MySQL Connector/J (included in the repository)

## Database Setup

1. Open MySQL.
2. Create the database:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE college_management_v2;
```

3. The application automatically creates the required tables when it connects to the database.

## Configuration

The application reads database credentials from environment variables.

Set the following variables on Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
$env:DB_USER="your_mysql_username"
$env:DB_PASSWORD="your_mysql_password"
```

Replace the placeholder values with your own local MySQL credentials.

## How to Run

1. Clone or download this repository.
2. Ensure MySQL Server is running.
3. Configure the database environment variables.
4. Open the project folder.
5. Run:

```powershell
.\run.bat
```

The script compiles the Java application and launches the College Management System.

## Security Note

This is an academic project. The current implementation stores application login passwords directly in the database. Secure password hashing should be implemented before using the application in a production environment.

## Project Status

Developed as an independent academic project to explore Java desktop application development, JDBC connectivity and relational database management.
